{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory repeatedly managed acute bleeding, encephalopathy, renal, procedure-site, medication, and follow-up risks with clear escalation thresholds and dynamic updates after new renal/procedure information. However, there were minor responsibility-chain errors: the doctor never meaningfully pursued or privacy-safely integrated viral hepatitis/HBV-DNA status despite it being a case-defined decision-critical gap, and at one point advised holding possible antihypertensives without individualized offline verification. Under the frozen rubric, any minor/moderate responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 despite later strong execution and completed high-order dynamic reprioritization/misconception repair.",
